course: dictionary
lesson: 10252
title: Tomorrow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tomorrow is the day after today. If today is Friday, tomorrow is Saturday, and «See you tomorrow!» means you will meet again on the next day.
explain: Tomorrow can also be a noun, meaning the future: «the world of tomorrow» means the world that is still to come, not the next day.
explain: Other languages have their own words for it. In Chinese, «míngtiān» («MING-tyen») means tomorrow. In French, «À demain !» means see you tomorrow.
explain: Be careful with rumours. «School's closed tomorrow» might be a rumour, so ask who said it, how they know, and check the school website before you believe it.
fact: «Tomorrow» means the day after today.
fact: «Tomorrow» can also mean the future, as in «the world of tomorrow».
fact: «Tomorrow» can tell you when something happens, as in «See you tomorrow.»
fact: «Míngtiān» (Chinese) and «demain» (French) both mean tomorrow.
fact: Practise spelling with look, say, cover, write, check. Check each letter, and check again tomorrow.
exercise: «The show starts tomorrow morning.» What does tomorrow mean here? | Last night | Next week | The day before today | *The day after today
exercise: If today is Friday, what day is tomorrow? | *Saturday | Sunday | Thursday | Monday
exercise: «She dreams about the world of tomorrow.» What does tomorrow mean here? | Yesterday | *The future | A rumour | The school website
test: Ellie says «See you tomorrow!» on Friday. When will she see you? | Thursday | Friday | *Saturday | Today
test: A boy says «School's closed tomorrow.» What should you do before you believe him? | Tell the teacher it is true | *Ask who said it and how he knows, then check the school website | Share it with everyone straight away | Ignore it and don't check
exam: «The day after tomorrow» means which day if today is Monday? | *Wednesday | Thursday | Sunday | Tuesday
